        "body": "OpenAI is a for-profit startup founded in 2015 and headquartered in San Francisco, CA, USA. Its website, chatgpt.com, describes ChatGPT as a tool to answer questions, write, create images, complete work, and code in one place. The site states that chats may be reviewed and used to improve AI models.\n\nOpenAI's products include ChatGPT, the OpenAI API and GPT models, the OpenAI Playground/Dashboard, Operator, DALL-E, Sora, and the Whisper API. These cover general chat, developer API access, autonomous web browsing, image generation, video generation, and speech recognition.\n\nOpenAI is named in federal litigation including United States v. OpenAI OpCo LLC, The Seattle Times Company v. OpenAI Inc., and wikiHow, Inc. v. OpenAI, Inc. California is listed as a jurisdiction with 281 law exposure entries. MCP servers associated with OpenAI include ai.com.mcp/openai-tools and several ai.getvda and ai.smithery agents.",
